---
/** Method: the documents, how the estimate is computed, its track record in 2026, the limits. Figures from the kit. */
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { route } from '../../i18n/routes';
import { KIT as K } from '../../lib/kit';
import { src, table } from '../../lib/helpers';
import { VALUE } from '../../content/home';
import { breadcrumbSchema, webPageSchema } from '../../lib/seo';
const lang = 'en';
const path = route('method', lang);
const E = K.E, L = E.LATEST, F = K.F.p95;
const title = 'Petrol Price Estimate Method 2026: CEF Data and Track Record';
const description = 'How the petrol price estimate is built in 2026: CEF daily over-recovery, projection to the close of the window, levy changes, and the test on every 2026 window.';
const bt = (rows: typeof K.BT.p95) => rows.map((r) => [K.day(r.effective), K.day(r.sheet), `${r.n} of ${r.N}`, K.dc(r.avg), K.dc(r.projected), K.dc(r.final)]);
---
<PageLayout title={title} description={description} lang={lang} jsonLd={[webPageSchema({ name: 'How the estimate is made', description, path, lang }), breadcrumbSchema([{ name: 'Home', path: route('home', lang) }, { name: 'How the estimate is made', path }])]} breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'How the estimate is made' }]}>
  <article class="prose prose-slate max-w-none prose-headings:font-serif">
    <h1>How the petrol price estimate is made</h1>
    <p><strong>The estimate takes the average over- or under-recovery the Central Energy Fund (CEF) publishes for the current window, fills the business days still to come with the latest daily figure, rounds the window average to the cent as the statement does, then adds the levy changes already announced. Every figure was read in the documents on {K.day(K.RETRIEVED)}.</strong></p>
    <p>{VALUE}</p>
    <h2>1. The documents read</h2>
    <p>The <Fragment set:html={src('cef_daily', 'Daily Basic Fuel Price sheets')} /> of the CEF, one PDF per business day: eleven sheets of 2026 were read, one after each price change, the latest dated {K.day(L.date)}. The <Fragment set:html={src('cef_2026', 'media statements of 2026')} />, eleven of them, with their Annexure 1: price changes, exchange rate, fuel levy, Road Accident Fund levy, slate levy, the final over- or under-recovery of each window, the full price structure in Gauteng, and the price history at each change since April 2024 ({E.HISTORY.length} rows). The CEF lists the monthly press release among the records available without a request in its <Fragment set:html={src('cef_paia', 'PAIA manual')} />; its pages carry an “All Rights Reserved” notice, so this site recalculates and cites the figures and never republishes the documents. Interest rates come from the public data service of the <Fragment set:html={src('sarb_rates', 'South African Reserve Bank')} />, read on {K.day(E.SARB_BUILT)}, and the meeting dates from its <Fragment set:html={src('sarb_mpc', 'Monetary Policy Committee page')} />.</p>
    <h2>2. The calculation</h2>
    <p>For each fuel: projected gap = (average to date × days so far + latest daily gap × days to come) ÷ days in the window. On {K.day(L.date)} the window had run {E.DAYS_SO_FAR} business days since {K.day(L.window[0])}; it is assumed to close on {K.day(E.WINDOW_END_ASSUMED)}, a Thursday six days before the change, as in eight of the nine windows of 2026, which gives {E.WINDOW_DAYS} days. For petrol 95: ({K.dc(L.average.p95)} × {E.DAYS_SO_FAR} + {K.dc(L.day.p95)} × {E.WINDOW_DAYS - E.DAYS_SO_FAR}) ÷ {E.WINDOW_DAYS} = {K.dc(F.projected)}, rounded to {K.dc(F.roundedRecovery)}. An over-recovery lowers the price by that amount; then the levy relief ending adds {K.dc(E.RELIEF.petrol)} on petrol and {K.dc(E.RELIEF.diesel)} on diesel. Result for 95: {K.dc(F.change)}, from {K.rpl(F.now)} to {K.rpl(F.next)} in Gauteng.</p>
    <p>The coastal price applies the Gauteng to coast gap of the latest price history (87c on petrol). Diesel and paraffin are wholesale prices. The paraffin shop maximum moves by {K.dec(E.SMNRP_RATIO, 2)} times the wholesale change, the average ratio of the 2026 statements. LPG is not estimated: no daily figure is published for it. The slate levy is kept unchanged unless you change it, because it depends on a balance published only with the statement.</p>
    <h2>3. Track record on the windows of 2026</h2>
    <p>For each window of 2026 with a CEF sheet near its middle, both ways of carrying the window forward were compared with the final figure of the statement. Method B, used on this site, missed by {K.dc(K.BT.mae95)} on average on petrol 95, against {K.dc(K.BT.maeAvg95)} for method A; on 500 ppm diesel, {K.dc(K.BT.mae50)} against {K.dc(K.BT.maeAvg50)}.</p>
    <Fragment set:html={table(['Change of', 'Sheet of', 'Days known', 'A: average', 'B: latest carried', 'Final'], bt(K.BT.p95), 'Petrol 95, cents a litre, positive = over-recovery.', ['l', 'l', 'r', 'r', 'r', 'r'])} />
    <Fragment set:html={table(['Change of', 'Sheet of', 'Days known', 'A: average', 'B: latest carried', 'Final'], bt(K.BT.d50), 'Diesel 500 ppm, cents a litre, positive = over-recovery.', ['l', 'l', 'r', 'r', 'r', 'r'])} />
    <h2>4. Interest rate calculations</h2>
    <p>Instalments use equal monthly payments at the annual rate divided by 12, with the rate unchanged over the term; fees, insurance and bond registration costs are left out. Scenarios of rate moves are illustrations, not forecasts of the committee’s decisions.</p>
    <h2>5. Limits</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>An estimate, not the official price: the Department’s statement a few days before each change gives the figures that apply.</li>
      <li>The figures are those of the documents read on {K.day(K.RETRIEVED)}; nothing on the site updates by itself, and each page shows the date of its data.</li>
      <li>A large move in oil prices or the rand before the window closes changes the result; the calculator lets you test one.</li>
      <li>Coastal prices of petrol 93 and 50 ppm diesel are not published; the site shows Gauteng only for them.</li>
      <li>Pump prices of diesel and paraffin depend on each station’s margin.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Corrections: <a href={route('contact', lang)}>contact page</a>.</p>
  </article>
</PageLayout>
